From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 212] panvk: decode transcoded BC ASTC planes at 8 bits per channel
Generated-by: LLM

Mali decodes LDR ASTC to fp16 in the texture cache unless the view asks
for 8-bit decode, and filters such texels at half rate (G615 counter
guide, "Texture full speed filtering percentage").  The ASTC planes that
BC1-BC3/BC7 UNORM images are transcoded to come from 8-bit data, so the
BC views now select narrow decode: full-rate bilinear and trilinear
filtering and half the texture cache footprint, at no precision cost.
sRGB views already decode narrow; HDR (BC6H) keeps fp16.  A biblioklept
reading at full speed.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/210

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_image_view.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_image_view.c
index 4837f180..a5ba6690 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_image_view.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_image_view.c
@@ -440,6 +440,11 @@ panvk_per_arch(CreateImageView)(VkDevice _device,
                         : panvk_bc_decoded_view_format(image->vk.format,
                                                        view->vk.view_format));
       view->pview.astc.hdr = util_format_is_astc_hdr(view->pview.format);
+      /* The transcoded LDR ASTC plane comes from 8-bit BC data, so decode it
+       * to 8 bits per channel: it then filters at full rate instead of the
+       * half rate of the default fp16 decode, and takes half the texture
+       * cache. pan_texture leaves sRGB views on their usual decode. */
+      view->pview.astc.narrow = !view->pview.astc.hdr;
       view->pview.planes[0] = (struct pan_image_plane_ref){
          .image = &image->bc_decoded.image,
          .plane_idx = 0,
